Constraints: 0 <= s.length <= 200 | s consists of English letters (lower-case and upper-case), digits (0-9), ' ', '+', '-', and '.'.

Approach: String to Integer Conversion with Edge Case Handling. The solution processes the string in three phases: whitespace trimming, sign detection, and digit conversion. It handles edge cases like leading zeros, out-of-range values, and invalid characters.

Algorithm: Trim leading whitespace characters from the string. Check for a sign character ('+' or '-') and record the sign. Skip leading zeros and read digits until a non-digit character is encountered or the end of the string is reached. Convert the collected digits to an integer, applying the sign. Clamp the result to the 32-bit signed integer range [-2^31, 2^31 - 1].

Correctness: The algorithm correctly handles all edge cases by trimming whitespace, detecting the sign, skipping leading zeros, and validating the numeric range. It ensures that invalid characters stop the conversion process and returns 0 if no valid digits are found.

Time: O(n), where n is the length of the string. Each character is processed once.. Space: O(1), as the algorithm uses a constant amount of extra space..

Java solution:
class Solution {
    public int myAtoi(String s) {
        int index = 0;
        int n = s.length();

        // Skip leading whitespace
        while (index < n && s.charAt(index) == ' ') {
            index++;
        }

        // Determine sign
        int sign = 1;
        if (index < n && s.charAt(index) == '-') {
            sign = -1;
            index++;
        } else if (index < n && s.charAt(index) == '+') {
            index++;
        }

        // Skip leading zeros
        while (index < n && s.charAt(index) == '0') {
            index++;
        }

        // Read digits
        int result = 0;
        while (index < n && Character.isDigit(s.charAt(index))) {
            int digit = s.charAt(index) - '0';

            // Check for overflow
            if (result > Integer.MAX_VALUE / 10 || (result == Integer.MAX_VALUE / 10 && digit > 7)) {
                return Integer.MAX_VALUE;
            }
            if (result < Integer.MIN_VALUE / 10 || (result == Integer.MIN_VALUE / 10 && digit > 8)) {
                return Integer.MIN_VALUE;
            }

            result = result * 10 + digit;
            index++;
        }

        return result * sign;
    }
}

