Approach: Three-Pointer In-Place Sorting. This solution uses a three-pointer approach to sort the array in-place with one pass and constant extra space. It maintains three pointers: low, mid, and high. The low pointer marks the boundary of 0s, the high pointer marks the boundary of 2s, and the mid pointer traverses the array. Based on the value at mid, we swap elements to place 0s at the beginning, 2s at the end, and 1s in the middle.

