Approach: Sliding Window with Hash Map. The solution uses a sliding window approach to find the minimum window in s that contains all characters of t, including duplicates. We maintain a count of characters in the current window and adjust the window size dynamically to find the minimum valid substring.

Algorithm: Initialize two pointers, left and right, to represent the current window in s. Use a hash map (or array) to track the frequency of characters in t and the current window. Expand the right pointer to include more characters until the window contains all characters of t. Once the window contains all characters of t, try to shrink the window from the left to find the minimum valid window. Update the minimum window length and its starting index whenever a valid window is found. Continue this process until the end of s is reached.

