Difficulty: Medium

Problem: Given strings s1, s2, and s3, find whether s3 is formed by an interleaving of s1 and s2.

An interleaving of two strings s and t is a configuration where s and t are divided into n and m substrings respectively, such that:

 s = s1 + s2 + ... + sn
 t = t1 + t2 + ... + tm
 |n - m| <= 1
 The interleaving is s1 + t1 + s2 + t2 + s3 + t3 + ... or t1 + s1 + t2 + s2 + t3 + s3 + ...

Note: a + b is the concatenation of strings a and b.

Example 1:

Input: s1 = "aabcc", s2 = "dbbca", s3 = "aadbbcbcac"
Output: true
Explanation: One way to obtain s3 is:
Split s1 into s1 = "aa" + "bc" + "c", and s2 into s2 = "dbbc" + "a".
Interleaving the two splits, we get "aa" + "dbbc" + "bc" + "a" + "c" = "aadbbcbcac".
Since s3 can be obtained by interleaving s1 and s2, we return true.

Example 2:

Input: s1 = "aabcc", s2 = "dbbca", s3 = "aadbbbaccc"
Output: false
Explanation: Notice how it is impossible to interleave s2 with any other string to obtain s3.

Example 3:

Input: s1 = "", s2 = "", s3 = ""
Output: true

Constraints:

 0 <= s1.length, s2.length <= 100
 0 <= s3.length <= 200
 s1, s2, and s3 consist of lowercase English letters.

Follow up: Could you solve it using only O(s2.length) additional memory space?

Constraints: 0 <= s1.length, s2.length <= 100 | 0 <= s3.length <= 200 | s1, s2, and s3 consist of lowercase English letters. | Follow up: Could you solve it using only O(s2.length) additional memory space?

Approach: Dynamic Programming with Space Optimization. We use dynamic programming to determine if s3 can be formed by interleaving s1 and s2. We optimize space by using a 1D DP array.

Algorithm: Check if the combined length of s1 and s2 equals the length of s3. If not, return false. Initialize a 1D boolean array dp of size (len(s2) + 1) to track valid interleavings. Set dp[0] = true since an empty string is always an interleaving. Iterate through each character in s3. For each position i in s3, update dp[j] based on whether the current character matches s1[i - j] or s2[j - 1]. Return dp[len(s2)] as the final result.

Correctness: The DP approach ensures that for each position in s3, we check all possible ways to form it by taking characters from s1 and s2. The space optimization ensures we use only O(len(s2)) space.

Time: O(n * m), where n is the length of s1 and m is the length of s2.. Space: O(m), where m is the length of s2..

Java solution:
class Solution {
    public boolean isInterleave(String s1, String s2, String s3) {
        int len1 = s1.length(), len2 = s2.length(), len3 = s3.length();
        if (len1 + len2 != len3) return false;
        boolean[] dp = new boolean[len2 + 1];
        dp[0] = true;
        for (int i = 0; i <= len3; i++) {
            for (int j = 0; j <= len2; j++) {
                int k = i - j;
                if (k < 0) continue;
                if (i == 0 && j == 0) continue;
                if (s3.charAt(i - 1) == s1.charAt(k - 1) && dp[j] && k > 0) {
                    dp[j] = true;
                } else if (s3.charAt(i - 1) == s2.charAt(j - 1) && dp[j - 1] && j > 0) {
                    dp[j] = true;
                }
            }
        }
        return dp[len2];
    }
